1
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,120
Brighten up the room and try stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:42,800
It'll all work out eventually, I'm sure.

3
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come over to my place.

4
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

5
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,240
Look, even Akaneru is burning up.
It'll all work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:27,440
You get it, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, shut up and follow me.

7
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,740
Battery Day?

8
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,600
Why is November 11th Battery Day?

9
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,640
If you write November 11th in kanji,

10
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:53,040
it comes out as plus,
minus, plus, minus, right?

11
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:56,520
To help people learn the
importance of electrical energy,

12
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,160
it's the day that was
established for that purpose.

13
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:02,320
Nakagawa Housing is also
commemorating that day

14
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,940
by holding an event.

15
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,240
Does that event have
prize money or something?

16
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:08,780
Prize money?

17
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,940
Let me see... what was it again?

18
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:11,620
Nakagawa.

19
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:12,340
Yes?

20
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,960
Take me to that event venue.

21
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,260
Stop your dawdling and complaining.

22
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:20,160
Alright, alright, I understand.

23
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:26,640
We've been expecting you, President.

24
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:30,200
This is our eco-housing development chief,

25
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:31,360
Mr. Matsunaga.

26
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,240
Pleased to meet you, pleased to meet you.

27
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:36,840
I'm Netaro Matsunaga.

28
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:37,440
Nice to meet you.

29
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,780
Matsunaga Netaro,
"Nerutto" for short, ha-ha, very modern.

30
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:41,760
Dad used to come up with things like that.

31
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,820
My motto is to cherish limited resources.

32
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:47,060
Please, take a look.

33
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:53,880
This is our latest creation, the solar house
"Himawari-kun."

34
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,780
It's just an ordinary house, isn't it?

35
00:02:55,780 --> 00:03:00,720
No, no,
this house actually rotates to face the sun.

36
00:03:00,720 --> 00:03:02,420
The house turns?

37
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:07,460
That way, sunlight always
shines through the whole house.

38
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:09,280
Doesn't it make you dizzy?

39
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,460
It only turns once a day,
so you barely notice it.

40
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:15,320
But it can't light up the
back of the house, can it?

41
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,840
For cases like that,

42
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,320
Mirror open!

43
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:33,020
It's like a transforming robot.

44
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,740
By adjusting the angle of the mirrors,

45
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:40,740
natural light reaches
every corner of the room.

46
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:45,060
With this, you'll be fine even if
you stay cooped up at home for a month.

47
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:46,740
Couldn't you just go outside?

48
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,340
Some people can't do that
because of their jobs.

49
00:03:50,680 --> 00:03:55,380
Many cases involve being holed up underground,
like recording sessions or anime voice-overs, right?

50
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,440
Why do you assume it has to be underground?

51
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,560
Why not do voice-overs on a
riverbank bathed in sunlight?

52
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,680
Manga artists can just
draw in the open air too.

53
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:09,240
In summer, it's a dream life where
you can get a tan while working.

54
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,740
But I think it'll be cold in winter.

55
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,300
Do you think so?

56
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:18,040
Imabari-kun and Miller-kun
are both recommended,

57
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:21,820
but our proudest creation is this one.

58
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:24,180
The ultimate energy-saving house.

59
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:28,200
It's the self-powered house,
Energy-Saving Jiro-kun.

60
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,220
The entire roof is solar panels.

61
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:37,240
Plus, wind turbines generate power, fully
covering the household's electricity use.

62
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:41,240
What happens if it's cloudy or rainy
and there's no wind for days on end?

63
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,040
Don't worry about it.

64
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,640
There's a bicycle inside the house,

65
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:47,260
why?

66
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,180
Don't tell me this is

67
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:51,260
yes, it's a charging system.

68
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,400
When sunlight or wind power isn't available,

69
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:04,680
you can easily generate
electricity like this.

70
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:10,360
In other words, this house can be
completely energy self-sufficient on its own.

71
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:13,240
This time, using this Eco-Jiro-kun,

72
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:15,960
we'll be holding an eco-house contest.

73
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,920
An eco-house contest?

74
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:19,720
Please, take a look.

75
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:29,620
The Decisive Battle!
The Energy-Saving House!

76
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:39,080
Battery Day Commemoration!
The First Energy-Saving House Contest!

77
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:46,660
For the next week, you will all compete
to see who can live the most energy-efficiently.

78
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,420
The winning team will receive

79
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:49,800
Get this,

80
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:53,720
that super-luxurious golden
energy-saving house as a prize!

81
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,540
Wow, amazing!

82
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:59,780
It's a product that's hard to tell whether
it's eco-friendly or just a waste of money.

83
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:03,240
Saving money is the field I'm best at.

84
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,560
The championship is as good as mine.

85
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:08,320
Why do we have to take part in this too?

86
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:09,420
That's right.

87
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:12,100
Nakagawa's the organizer,
so he can't take part.

88
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:15,940
Plus, every team has to
include at least one woman.

89
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:18,660
Already falling out among yourselves?

90
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,780
Come on, Gonji, Volvo, Jordy.

91
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:23,440
Hey there, long time no see!

92
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:25,700
Sorry, but the win is ours.

93
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:30,240
And we'll turn that house
into Meatbobby's sweet home.

94
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:31,640
Aaaaah!

95
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,700
Let's talk about that later, at our leisure.

96
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:37,680
Where are you going, Bobby?

97
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:41,500
Can we really live together in that place?

98
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:45,260
But a formidable rival
has joined the competition!

99
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,740
Here, Yo-chan-kichi.

100
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:51,420
Komachi-chan, Naoko-chan, Maria-chan,
are all of you going to participate too?

101
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:55,020
Yes, though I'll end up
being rivals with Reiko-san.

102
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:57,680
I'm definitely not losing to you,
of all people!

103
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:58,380
What's your problem?

104
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,700
Lord Ryo.

105
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:04,560
No matter who wins,
let's live together in that house, shall we?

106
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,380
How did it come to that?

107
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:11,360
Looks like we've come to the wrong place.

108
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:17,460
For the next week,
you will all live according to a timetable.

109
00:07:17,460 --> 00:07:21,660
First, each team will be given 3,000 yen.

110
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:26,820
Gas, water, meal costs and so on will
be calculated and displayed on the roof.

111
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,520
The electricity you generate
will be added to this as well.

112
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,640
When the game ends,
the team with the most money left wins.

113
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:41,240
If your pension drops to zero or you break the schedule,
you will be disqualified, so please be careful.

114
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:46,580
Then, the Battery Day Commemorative
Eco-House Contest begins!

115
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:50,780
The participants all
enter their houses at once.

116
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:52,840
The first hour is free time.

117
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,260
I wonder how each team
will spend their time.

118
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:59,060
Naoko, turn off the lights in all the rooms.

119
00:07:59,060 --> 00:07:59,720
Got it.

120
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,900
Maria, open the curtains.

121
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:02,400
Yes.

122
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:06,540
Ugh, we have to make sure the
car doesn't waste any electricity.

123
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:11,000
I've turned off all the lights
and opened the curtains. Thanks!

124
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:20,340
No way, why is electricity still flowing? I checked again for anything left on,
and found it.

125
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:27,800
Everything's off.
I haven't forgotten to switch anything off.

126
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:34,780
W-why? What's going on?
Isn't this machine broken?

127
00:08:34,780 --> 00:08:40,260
You fools! Most household
appliances draw standby power,

128
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:43,380
so they use electricity even
when you're doing nothing.

129
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:48,240
Senpai, I've unplugged the fridge,
the microwave, and the washing machine.

130
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:50,420
I've unplugged the computer too.

131
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:51,300
Good.

132
00:08:53,260 --> 00:08:54,960
Good, it stopped dead.

133
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:56,360
Truly the king of thrift.

134
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:16,800


135
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,240
Honda, hurry up!

136
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,900
What? Do I have to do it too?

137
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:22,680
Of course.

138
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:26,420
Look, I went to the trouble
of modifying it just for you.

139
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,440
Is this a motorcycle?

140
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:29,840
Hurry up and get on.

141
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,420
Fine, fine.

142
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,460
There's no way it's running
on something like this.

143
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:41,880
That's it, keep it up!

144
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:43,500
Reiko, don't slack off either.

145
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,980
Got it?

146
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:48,560
Ryo-san's team isn't losing either.

147
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:51,020
The other teams are also
working hard to make it happen.

148
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,840
Phew, I'm exhausted.

149
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,980
I'm parched.

150
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,520
Wait.

151
00:10:00,780 --> 00:10:02,140
Take a good look.

152
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:06,140
We're saving it up one drop at a time.

153
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:09,280
Why one drop at a time?

154
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:11,220
So the water meter doesn't turn.

155
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:12,380
We can drink it for free.

156
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:14,440
But it takes a long time, you know.

157
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:16,920
Yeah, one cup isn't expensive, you know.

158
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:20,400
Naive! That one cup is the
start of our total collapse!

159
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,100
It's just like dieting!

160
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:26,200
I'll manage all the food and drinks,
understand?

161
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:29,060
I'll go fetch some river water now.

162
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,400
Senpai, you're serious, aren't you.

163
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:34,100
Looks like we're in for a tough life.

164
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:37,020
Lunchtime is getting close.

165
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:40,300
Please buy whatever you need at
the supermarket inside the venue.

166
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:43,000
The cost will be deducted
from your electricity.

167
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:50,620
Terai's team just went out shopping. Apparently,
since they have kids, they're short on mealtime, it seems.

168
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:53,140
I bought it, dammit!

169
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,120
Here you go.

170
00:11:01,580 --> 00:11:04,620
One each. Take your own.

171
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:10,120
It's like we're living on a desert island.

172
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:13,240
This is more survival than saving money,
isn't it.

173
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:17,760
Hey, I'm so thirsty I don't think I can eat.

174
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,220
Has the water built up?

175
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,140
Not yet.

176
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,880
What are we going to do?
I can't take it anymore.

177
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,640
Me too.

178
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,920
Don't worry.

179
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:29,120
I'll filter the river water right now.

180
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,440
You're going to drink that? Seriously?

181
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:37,980
Here.

182
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,120
It's kind of brownish.

183
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,540
Don't worry about it.

184
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,480
I drank some too, and nothing happened.

185
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:48,440
Don't compare me to Ryo-chan's stomach,
the human garbage disposal!

186
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,480
Senpai, please.

187
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:53,780
Please, just one cup of water.

188
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,560
Fine, I suppose.

189
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:58,280
Just one cup, got it?

190
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:01,780
Here, one cup of water.

191
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:09,540
Night has fallen.

192
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:12,320
The meter is running
because we're using lights.

193
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,140
It's dark, isn't it.

194
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:18,440
One fluorescent light is enough.

195
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,820
Darker is more relaxing

196
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:23,620
It's almost time for bathing.

197
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:25,940
Each team, please get ready.

198
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:32,880
We left the water in a sunny spot to warm it up,
didn't we?

199
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:37,040
This way, we won't have to pay
for electricity either, right?

200
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:42,840
I don't really like this
sort of thing, but...

201
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,900
There's no helping it at this point.

202
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,240
This way, we'll need less hot water, so.

203
00:12:55,020 --> 00:12:58,780
Bobby, if three of us bathe together,
we'll need even less.

204
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,680
Bobby, what's wrong?

205
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,280
Kuro-dan, the water's going to overflow!

206
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:18,840
Senpai, this doesn't really
count as taking a bath, does it?

207
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:22,200
Besides, it's almost all water,
and we'll catch a cold.

208
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:26,300
Bear with it.
Heating uses the most electricity, you know.

209
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:30,980
If you don't get in up to your shoulders,
you're disqualified.

210
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:32,560
I'm just about to get in.

211
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,780
See? I'm in up to my shoulders, all right.

212
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,140
But the water temperature seems quite low.

213
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,500
That's not true.

214
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,040
Besides, this guy likes lukewarm water.

215
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:48,600
As for me,

216
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:50,020
I like it, don't I?

217
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:51,360
It's fine.

218
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:53,980
It's nice, isn't it.

219
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,860
No complaints, right?

220
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:59,940
Currently in first place is Team Sakonji.

221
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:01,540
Second place is Team Ryotsu.

222
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:02,860
The contest is still early.

223
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:04,740
It'll be exciting to see how things develop.

224
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:22,180
I wonder where Ryo-chan went.

225
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:27,100
There was tap water in a plastic bottle,
wasn't there?

226
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:31,820
I wonder where it is. I hid it somewhere.

227
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:39,640
"If it's just the two of us, we'll drink it because we can't hold back."
You really did hit the nail on the head.

228
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:42,060
Right, I've bought some food!

229
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:49,420
Today's a feast!
Well then, fish sausage it is.

230
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:52,260
Just one bite?

231
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,860
I went to the trouble of buying it for you,
and you have a complaint?

232
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:57,500
No, maybe that was a bit too much.

233
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:00,240
Look at the Volvo team.

234
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:03,740
They have 150 yen's worth
more electricity than we do!

235
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:08,560
Those guys don't turn on any lights at night.
They live in total darkness.

236
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:12,880
On top of that, they get their food by hunting,
so their food costs are zero.

237
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:16,300
I wonder what on earth
they're catching and eating.

238
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:20,100
But in that case,
we don't stand a chance, do we?

239
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:25,260
Don't worry,
by my reckoning it should be around tonight.

240
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,260
Calm down.

241
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:28,140
Just forget it already.

242
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:29,580
Wait, Sakonji.

243
00:15:29,580 --> 00:15:31,640
I don't want to eat that stuff anymore.

244
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:33,700
It's just one more night. Hang in there.

245
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,780
At least let me play video games.

246
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:38,360
No way. A color TV uses a ton of power.

247
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,680
Uh-oh.

248
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:43,220
Volvo and Jodie might be able to handle it,

249
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:45,120
but Sakonji couldn't.

250
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:55,920
Chance! We're charging the battery, now!
Are you really doing this? Then at least let me take a bath.
The floor's a mess. You just don't want to bathe yourself, do you?

251
00:15:55,920 --> 00:16:03,020
Who'd bathe in that murky river water?
People don't die from not bathing!

252
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:10,900
That's just how it is, isn't it?
This is turning into more of a spectator thing.
Well, the contest is reaching its climax!

253
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:13,160
And now, it's event time!

254
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:16,680
Team representatives,
please gather on stage.

255
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:19,040
Event time?

256
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:25,800
Now, please each draw one card.

257
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:31,340
This is

258
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:34,220
What?

259
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:40,000
The Komachi team drew the card where
neighborhood kids come over to play.

260
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:42,020
So what, then!

261
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,500
Arai?

262
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:47,020
Hah!

263
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:47,600
Hah!

264
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:47,640
Hah!

265
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:48,940
Hah!

266
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:51,540
W-what in the world is going on here?

267
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:52,880
Let us watch TV!

268
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:54,600
There's a computer too!

269
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:55,160
Let's play a game!

270
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:58,460
Stop that, the electricity!

271
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:03,365
A plain savings contest
wouldn't be much fun, so

272
00:17:03,415 --> 00:17:05,540
we added a game element.

273
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,500
It's just like the Game of Life.

274
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:09,980
Next team, please draw a card.

275
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:11,700
Uuugh...

276
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,640
Hup!

277
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,040
Gah, this is...

278
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:19,880
We drew the Sakonji team's
electrical store inspection card.

279
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:23,460
Excuse me, we've come to inspect
your electrical appliances.

280
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:26,040
Stop it!

281
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,920
Nothing's broken anywhere.

282
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,920
Pasarin will thoroughly check
every electrical appliance.

283
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,580
And all the electricity we
worked so hard to save...

284
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:38,840
With this event, the Sakonji team is
going to drop in the rankings all at once.

285
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:41,480
If only we knew what was in that card...

286
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:51,100
What's going on?

287
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:54,400
Could it be a power outage?

288
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:56,740
Someone go check!

289
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:11,860
Eeeeeh, what a shitty card!

290
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:19,960
Lucky card or not, it's a waste on a thunderbolt like you.
I'll take this one.

291
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:28,640
Sorry about that. Let's continue.
The card Terai's team drew is...

292
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,100
Uuuugh.

293
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:37,880
Smokebear's young guys drew the
card where visitors come to play.

294
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:50,600
We suddenly have to cook
a huge amount of food.

295
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:52,560
This is a big blow.

296
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:53,780
No way.

297
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,180
Then, next team.

298
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,320
Wait.

299
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,120
I'll take this one.

300
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,740
Finally, this card came up.

301
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:11,320
The card both teams
drew is the Unlucky card.

302
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:12,780
Bad luck.

303
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:15,180
What, "unlucky"?

304
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:17,840
It's true.

305
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,920
This is the worst card.

306
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:23,940
Both teams will have their
electricity cut down to 100 yen's worth.

307
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:24,560
What?

308
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:33,100
Oh no! We've plunged straight to last place!

309
00:19:45,900 --> 00:19:47,980
In that case, we'll use our secret weapon.

310
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,940
Alright, go!

311
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,440
Boo, boo!

312
00:20:13,320 --> 00:20:14,420
Alright, next one.

313
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,840
Why has our electricity dropped so much?

314
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:39,100
The power lines are being chewed by rats.

315
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,260
There must be a short circuit.

316
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:42,500
I never expected rats to show up.

317
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:45,340
That's never happened before, though.

318
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:50,240
Why is your place the only one that's fine?

319
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,560
That's suspicious.

320
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:55,440
I took proper precautions
against rats at my place.

321
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:59,360
Besides, mine isn't the only
one that was spared, you know.

322
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:00,380
That's...

323
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:05,040
Still, it's odd that only
the top teams are getting hit.

324
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,840
What do we do, President?

325
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,920
There's no proof that the senior did it.

326
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:12,340
We have no choice but to carry on.

327
00:21:17,340 --> 00:21:19,360
I'll turn this around on our own strength.

328
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:22,180
Each team has entered its final push.

329
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,660
But there's only a little time left.

330
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:27,340
Useless, useless, the championship is mine!

331
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:30,620
I've claimed the golden
eco-house for myself!

332
00:21:36,780 --> 00:21:38,120
I've reached my limit.

333
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:42,220
What's wrong, Reiko?

334
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:44,940
I'm going to take a bath.

335
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:45,980
What?

336
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:49,640
Wait, Reiko!

337
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,520
Hey, open up!

338
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:52,360
Reiko...

339
00:21:52,360 --> 00:21:56,600
That feels good.

340
00:21:57,220 --> 00:21:59,340
Whoa, stop it!

341
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:02,600
Hot water uses the most electricity!

342
00:22:03,140 --> 00:22:03,580
Ugh.

343
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:04,420
Shhh...

344
00:22:07,260 --> 00:22:08,220
Whoa!

345
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:10,680
What are you doing, Reiko?

346
00:22:12,380 --> 00:22:15,980
This is so refreshing.
This is what human life is about!

347
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:20,120
Both teams' electricity
has suddenly started to drop!

348
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:23,700
What on earth is happening
inside the house right now?

349
00:22:23,700 --> 00:22:26,880
Uuugh, damn it!

350
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:28,240
Honda!

351
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:30,960
No good, it's useless now.

352
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,260
Now it's the final run!

353
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:36,820
Both teams have dropped in the rankings,
and the top spots are nearly neck and neck.

354
00:22:36,820 --> 00:22:38,660
Who's going to win?

355
00:22:38,660 --> 00:22:42,020
Damn it!
We've come this far, we're not losing now!

356
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:43,540
Yeah!

357
00:22:45,680 --> 00:22:47,960
Come on, five seconds left!

358
00:22:52,160 --> 00:22:55,220
God, give me electricity!

359
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:12,940
Senpai

360
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:15,780
The victory is mine.

361
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:19,360
Calling down lightning, too. How terrifying.

362
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:21,080
What an incredible obsession.

363
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:26,780
And now, the winning team of the first
Shoene House Contest will be announced.

364
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:30,880
The winner is...

365
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:34,680
Terai's team!

366
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:38,980
That's ridiculous!

367
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:40,260
I can't believe it.

368
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:42,080
The victory is mine.

369
00:23:42,080 --> 00:23:43,340
I saw it.

370
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:46,260
All the counters maxed out!

371
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:48,180
A momentary spike isn't enough.

372
00:23:48,180 --> 00:23:49,320
You're disqualified.

373
00:23:49,320 --> 00:23:50,460
N-no way...

374
00:23:52,160 --> 00:23:54,960
We were just living normally, though.

375
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:56,980
After all, he's always disappearing.

376
00:23:57,820 --> 00:23:58,620
Damn it.

377
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:01,760
What was all my effort for?

378
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:20,460
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone was calling out

379
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:27,160
I walked while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja

380
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:33,960
That strange feeling I had back then

381
00:24:35,620 --> 00:24:39,580
So on the arcade street's tiles

382
00:24:39,580 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones

383
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:51,520
Everyone was a child once,

384
00:24:51,520 --> 00:24:53,480
but everyone has forgotten

385
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:57,620
the politicians with
their self-important faces,

386
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:00,980
and the thorn-in-your-side aunties too

387
00:25:00,980 --> 00:25:03,960
Go on, try turning

388
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:06,560
at that corner

389
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:11,960
See you all, everyone!

390
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:12,740
Don't go!

391
00:25:12,740 --> 00:25:16,380
Over there is Kameari.

392
00:25:16,380 --> 00:25:19,720
Well, surely it's Kameari.

393
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:24,980
Everyone, come to our town!

394
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

395
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:34,760
Damn it, a dog, a mere pet, at that!

396
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:38,240
The world's gone wrong, a dog's
living several levels better than me!

397
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,560
If that's how it is, I'll become a dog too

398
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:43,160
and enjoy a blissful pet life!

399
00:25:43,600 --> 00:25:47,120
Next time, Ryo-san's dog life,
see you there!

400
00:25:59,420 --> 00:26:00,820
Thank you.

